    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1758" root="بثق" body-key="b">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَاثِقٌ</span></b>  [act. part. n. of 1]. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَكِيَّةٌ بَاثِقَةٌ</span> <i>A well
full, and abundant in water.</i> (K.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِيَاهٌ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُثَّقٌ</span> [pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَاثِقٌ</span>], like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُكَّعٌ</span> [pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَاكِعٌ</span>, app.
<i>Waters flowing forth abundantly</i>]. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3- 
[Hence,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُوَ بَاثِقُ الكَرَمِ</span> (assumed tropical:)  <i>He is abundant in generosity.</i> (K.)

